From: Onigiri
Subject: [PATCH] Fit the PIN pad on the cover

The 748x720 cover counts as landscape for resources but shows the lock
screen at rotation 0, so Samsung used the portrait bouncer with the Fold5
cover's landscape key sizes. Keys, message, PIN dots and emergency call were
taller than the screen, which cut off the message, the dots and the top row,
and put the lock icon on the 2 key.

KeyguardSecPINView now lays itself out on the cover before every measure
(OnigiriCoverPin): the message and the PIN dots share the lock icon's row,
the keypad fills the middle with keys up to 54 dp, and emergency call sits
at the bottom. With swipe navigation the view flipper keeps no bottom margin
and emergency call takes the strip left of the cameras; with buttons it goes
full width above the navigation bar and the keys shrink to fit. A message
too long for its half of the row shrinks, and the hint below it is dropped,
as Samsung's own landscape layout does.

diff --git a/smali/com/android/keyguard/KeyguardSecPINView.smali b/smali/com/android/keyguard/KeyguardSecPINView.smali
--- a/smali/com/android/keyguard/KeyguardSecPINView.smali
+++ b/smali/com/android/keyguard/KeyguardSecPINView.smali
@@ -42,6 +42,17 @@
     return-void
 .end method
 
+.method protected onMeasure(II)V
+    .locals 0
+
+    # Onigiri: lay the PIN pad out for the Flip5 cover before measuring (see OnigiriCoverPin).
+    invoke-static {p0, p1, p2}, Lcom/android/keyguard/OnigiriCoverPin;->fit(Landroid/view/View;II)V
+
+    invoke-super {p0, p1, p2}, Lcom/android/keyguard/KeyguardPINView;->onMeasure(II)V
+
+    return-void
+.end method
+
 .method public final onFinishInflate()V
     .locals 8
 
